---
// Day 3 Task 9 (02 §3): the agent courtesies the comment above used to defer
// -- /llms.txt (the curated index) and the MCP endpoint. /llms-full.txt is
// deliberately NOT linked here: it is the bulk-ingestion corpus and
// /llms.txt already points at it (task-9-brief.md Step 3), so a footer link
// to both would be redundant, and a footer link to the raw corpus is not a
// courtesy to a human visitor scanning the colophon. The `.md` variant
// routes (Task 7) have no single URL to link -- they are discoverable
// page-by-page via each HTML page's own <link rel="alternate">.
//
// Fix round 1 (task-9-report.md): the MCP link is `/mcp` on that domain, not
// the bare origin -- the custom domain is only the host,
// `workers/mcp/src/index.ts`'s `createMcpHandler(..., { route: '/mcp' })`
// mounts the actual JSON-RPC endpoint at that path, and the bare origin
// 404s. Verified live: POST https://mcp.ryanlindsey.me/mcp with an
// `initialize` body succeeds.
const year = new Date().getFullYear();
---

<footer data-site-footer class="mt-24 border-t border-rule">
  <div
    class="mx-auto flex max-w-5xl flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-4 px-6 py-8 font-mono text-micro uppercase text-ink-muted"
  >
    <span>&copy; {year} Ryan Lindsey</span>
    <!--
      2026-09 redesign (issue #99, note 5): /ops and /ai-policy left the
      primary nav for the footer -- demoted, not deleted, because they are
      about the site rather than part of reading it. This bare nav is a
      minimal landing spot, not the five-column SITE / SYSTEM / FOR AGENTS /
      ELSEWHERE footer the redesign eventually wants; that shape is a
      separate issue, and this placement is provisional until it lands.
    -->
    <nav aria-label="System" class="flex items-baseline gap-4">
      <a href="/ops">Ops</a>
      <a href="/ai-policy">AI Policy</a>
    </nav>
    <nav aria-label="Agent resources" class="flex items-baseline gap-4">
      <!-- Day 6 (04 §1) put /chat first here, in the footer rather than the
        primary nav, because it was the one agent-facing link a person could
        use without knowing what an MCP endpoint is. The 2026-09 redesign
        (issue #99) promoted it into the primary nav instead -- reachable
        from every page either way, only where from changed -- so it no
        longer duplicates here. -->
      <a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a>
      <a href="https://mcp.ryanlindsey.me/mcp">MCP</a>
    </nav>
    <span>Built on Cloudflare Workers &middot; Astro</span>
  </div>
</footer>
